# The enumeration succeeds and returns nothing

Round 1 of #1905 (NEW-6), the quieter half. `git ls-files` exits 0 with no
output whenever the pathspec matches nothing — a wrong pathspec, a repository
with an empty index, a checkout the hook did not expect. Exit status alone does
not separate that from a healthy sweep.

`repo: untracked` initializes the repository and adds nothing, so the file on
disk is real and the index is empty. A guard that only checks `git`'s exit
status passes this.
